    "label": "thm:main",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "For any randomized player strategy that relies on bandit feedback, there exists a sequence of loss functions $\\ell_1,\\ldots,\\ell_T$ (where $\\ell_t:[k] \\mapsto [0,1]$) that incurs a regret of $R = \\widetilde \\Omega(k^{1/3} T^{2/3})$, provided that $k \\le T$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Regret is expected (over player randomization) regret including switching costs vs best fixed action in hindsight. Also holds with binary losses (Sec 5.1)."
  },
